WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.759 --> 00:00:05.049
The new HBO series inspired by the classic
comic book series Watchmen has been shrouded

00:00:05.049 --> 00:00:09.260
in mystery thus far, with stories and characters
kept largely under wraps.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.200
While we wait to learn the truth, here's a
look at everything we know and think we know.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:18.600
Rumors about Lost co-creator Damon Lindelof
wanting to develop a Watchmen series brewed

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:24.420
as early as 2014, but it wasn't until August
2018 that Variety reported HBO had officially

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:25.820
given the show the greenlight.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:30.780
In November 2017, at Vulture Festival L.A.,
Lindelof talked to The Good Place creator

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.380
Mike Schur about his motivations for developing
the series, saying,

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.500
"Watchmen it was dangerous…the reason that
I'm doing this is these are dangerous times,

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.089
and we need dangerous shows."

00:00:40.089 --> 00:00:45.679
In May 2018, Lindelof posted a five-page letter
on Instagram addressed to Watchmen fans, retelling

00:00:45.679 --> 00:00:50.339
pieces of his own life story in the non-linear
style in which we learn the story of Dr. Manhattan

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.359
in Watchmen #4.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:55.960
He went on to describe his vision as not so
much an adaptation as a "remix" of the original

00:00:55.969 --> 00:01:00.309
story likening the comic book series to the
Bible's Old Testament and his series to the

00:01:00.309 --> 00:01:01.309
New Testament.

00:01:02.309 --> 00:01:06.270
So far, the only major character from the
comics confirmed to appear in the series is

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:10.760
the mastermind Ozymandias, played by Jeremy
Irons, and he's clearly much older than he

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.040
was in the original story.

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:15.800
There's also the cult of Rorschach, but it's
doubtful the original is among them.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.190
The other masked characters all appear brand
new.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:22.480
The question still remains: If the events
of the HBO Watchmen series take place after

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.990
the events of the comic book series, then
did things unfold as they did in the comic

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:26.660
book series?

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:31.060
For example, did Ozymandias' plan conclude
with the appearance of the artificial alien

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:34.970
like in the comics, or with the faked Dr.
Manhattan assault on New York City from Zack

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:35.970
Snyder's film?

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:38.120
And what happened to the other characters
from the comic?

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:45.080
In May 2018, The Hollywood Reporter revealed
that Regina King, Louis Gossett Jr., Don Johnson,

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:49.390
Adelaide Clemens, Tim Blake Nelson, and Andrew
Howard had been cast in the series pilot,

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:50.920
and that King would be the lead.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:53.500
There was no information about who the actors
would be playing...

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.600
"I can't say anything!"

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:56.180
"You really can't?"

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.510
"You might disappear if I do!"

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:03.430
...but since-released images, a leaked character
breakdown, the trailer, and the series' IMDb

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:04.780
page, has shed some light.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.820
King's character is Angela Abraham, who will
be one of the series' masked vigilantes, it

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:09.320
seems.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.159
She wears black leather clothing, including
a hooded jacket and a white shirt.

00:02:13.159 --> 00:02:16.150
A greyish-black material covers the bottom
half of her face.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:20.079
In the trailer, she also pins what appears
to be a police badge to her outfit.

00:02:20.079 --> 00:02:24.510
Nelson is listed on IMDb with the name Looking
Glass, making it seem likely he's playing

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.280
the vigilante with the reflective mask.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:30.800
Most of the others are listed with what appear
to be vigilante codenames: Clemens is Pirate

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:33.660
Jenny, Howard is Red Scare, and Gossett is
Old Man.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:37.360
Johnson's as-yet-unnamed character is one
of the most prominently featured in the trailer,

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:40.500
and it seems likely he plays a high-ranking
police officer.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:44.430
A leaked character breakdown mentions a woman
who is "wife of the police chief, Judd."

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:48.240
If the breakdown is to be believed, there's
a good chance Judd is Johnson's character.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:55.610
In June 2018, Deadline reported Yahya Abdul-Mateen
II had been added to HBO's Watchmen cast,

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:59.790
and it won't be Mateen's first role in a superhero
production; he was the vengeful antagonist

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.220
Black Manta in Aquaman.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:05.780
While not a lot is known about his role so
far, Abdul-Mateen's character Cal Abraham

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.820
appears to be the husband of Angela Abraham.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:11.660
He's listed as her stay-at-home husband in
a leaked character breakdown, and a shot in

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:14.500
the first Watchmen teaser trailer shows the
two embracing.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:15.540
"Are we safe?"

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:21.740
In January 2018, seasoned television director
Nicole Kassell was confirmed as director of

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:25.560
the Watchmen's pilot, as well as executive
producer for the series.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.510
Kassell directed two episodes of Lindelof's
The Leftovers, and she's had steady directing

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:34.499
work since her first TV directorial credit
for an episode of the CBS medical drama 3

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.000
lbs.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.500
Much of that work includes credits on successful,
acclaimed shows such as The Closer, Castle

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.920
Rock, Better Call Saul, The Killing, Westworld,
and The Americans, among others.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.100
HBO's official Watchmen Instagram account
has been a wealth of cryptic but interesting

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:49.600
reveals.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:53.200
Many images are little more than production
photos, but there are some more intriguing

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.510
images, including short videos referencing
the original Watchmen or simply showing us

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.120
a slice of this alternate America.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.780
One video shows an altered U.S. flag flapping
in the breeze, while another shows the skull-and-bones

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:07.730
pirate flag we briefly see in the trailer
that reminds any Watchmen reader of the "Tales

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:09.650
of the Black Freighter" pirate story.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:13.510
Yet another video shows what appears to be
Regina King's vigilante character walking

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:17.940
toward a police officer and one briefly shows
her unmasked, looking distressed.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.380
One more clip begins with two armed police
officers and cuts to Jeremy Irons as Ozymandias...

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:24.880
"It's only just begun."

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:29.820
...while another shows the aging superhero
blowing out a single candle on a birthday

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:30.320
cake.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:35.620
In the Watchmen comic, Rorschach is a mentally
unstable vigilante who believes in taking

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:37.540
extreme measures for the greater good.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:41.040
He's killed by Dr. Manhattan, but we soon
learn he's arranged for his journal to be

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:45.190
mailed to a right-wing publication, the New
Frontiersman, in the hopes that Ozymandias'

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:46.420
plot would be revealed.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:50.570
The story's final page takes place in the
Frontiersman office, where an exhausted editor

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:54.880
tells his assistant to pick a piece of reader
mail from an overflowing pile, where Rorschach's

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:57.300
journal sits, and to run a story based on
it.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:02.200
"Um, well, I guess something from the crank
file."

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.590
What seems to be a fanatical group based on
Rorschach exists in the future-set series,

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:10.850
strongly implying the vigilante's journal
and its revelations did see the light of day.

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:15.160
Yet the New Frontiersman is portrayed as a
small fringe publication, so there's no guarantee

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:19.440
any story it ran would be received as anything
more than a conspiracy theory by society at

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:19.940
large.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:24.460
This new pack of Rorschachs may very well
be culled from Frontiersman readers and like-minded

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:25.540
conspiracy theorists.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:31.040
Another Watchmen cast member came to light
in January 2019 when it was announced Good

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:33.180
Trouble's Dustin Ingram would join the show.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:37.490
Bleeding Cool spotted a brief reveal about
Ingram's Watchmen character buried in a story

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:42.340
about Ingram being cast in Amazon's upcoming
Utopia: Deadline offhandedly pointed out that

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:47.410
in Watchmen, Ingram will play, quote, "Agent
Petey, a junior FBI agent, with a vast knowledge

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.060
of the vigilantes (the Watchmen)."

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:53.740
Is Petey an expert on the new vigilantes like
Looking Glass and Regina Park's masked character,

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:57.940
or does his expertise revolve around Rorschach,
Nite Owl and the other comic characters?

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:01.880
Deadline's parenthetical mention of "the Watchmen"
doesn't help much, because in the comic book

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:03.930
series, "Watchmen" is not a team name.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.390
None of the heroes refer to themselves as
Watchmen.

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:10.380
The title comes from the work of the Roman
poet Juvenal, whose most famous line can be

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:13.300
translated from Latin, "Who watches the watchmen?"

